<h2>
The Antibiotic Resistance Connection
</h2>

<p>
Antibiotics are designed to affect microorganisms.
When antibiotic residues reach environmental waters,
they become part of a complex system involving
bacteria, genes and microbial communities.
</p>

<ul class="resistance-list">

<li>Antibiotic residues can occur in wastewater.</li>

<li>Wastewater contains diverse microbial communities.</li>

<li>Environmental exposure is studied as one factor
in antimicrobial resistance.</li>

<li>Responsible antibiotic use is important for protecting
their effectiveness.</li>

</ul>

</div>


<div class="resistance-visual">

<div class="big">🦠</div>

<h3>
Protect the effectiveness of medicines
</h3>

<p>
Use antibiotics responsibly and only when prescribed
or recommended by a qualified healthcare professional.
</p>

